# A plot after a reload (cmdref: PGD; Prescription I/O) and the NEW/parser units test, on the manual's Cassegrain.in.
# (pp) giza's PGQINF('DEV/TYPE') appended at most FOUR characters of the type name, so '/null' came back '/nul':
#   GRAINI caches that string after the first PGBEGIN, OLD closes the device (GRAEND), and the next plot's PGBEGIN
#   printed '%giza - ERROR - giza_open_device: Unknown device, device not opened' and every later plot drew nothing
#   (macos-fd 2026-10-19, in four regenerated dialogs).  /png (four characters) never showed it.
# (qq) 'BaseUnits= none' (and 'in') were tested against WaveUnits in both the NEW dialog and the parser, so a deck
#   or an answer giving one of the listed choices printed 'Unknown units, unitless operation assumed'.
# COPY: $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/Cassegrain.in
cd $TMP
old Cassegrain.in
opd 5
/null
old Cassegrain.in
opd 5
opd 5
! perl -i -pe 's/^(\s*)zSource=/$1BaseUnits= none\n$1zSource=/' Cassegrain.in
old Cassegrain.in
! perl -i -pe 's/BaseUnits= none/BaseUnits= in/' Cassegrain.in
old Cassegrain.in
opd 5
# EXPECT: (RMS OPD error is\s+\d\.\d+D-1[2-9][\s\S]*?){4}
# EXPECT-NOT: giza_open_device: Unknown device
# EXPECT-NOT: Unknown units
# EXPECT-NOT: Default used for BaseUnits[\s\S]*?Default used for BaseUnits[\s\S]*?Default used for BaseUnits
# EXPECT-NOT: forrtl
